{"type":"text","timestamp":1794589787269,"sessionID":"ses_e2a2563f6ffeukYbtxx7FqbjhX","part":{"id":"prt_1d5e2e4d4002bxDDRBwJiPs4te","sessionID":"ses_e2a2563f6ffeukYbtxx7FqbjhX","messageID":"msg_1d5e2c3d7001xWegUY1C1trtuO","type":"text","text":"T014's code change is in place in both named files, but the authoritative verify is blocked by a stale built dist from other lanes' `lib/` edits, and the plan forbids workers to build.\n\n**Files written**\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`: added the nine-name `PROJECTED_ENV` list, `readProjectedEnv()`, `envBefore`/`envAfter` capture around `scoreCommandCorpus()` in `beforeAll`, and the case `leaves the caller environment as it found it`.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`: added `PROJECTED_ENV_NAMES`, saved each value or absence before the `try`, and restored or deleted each name in the `finally` immediately after `globalThis.Date = RealDate;`.\n\n**Verify output**\n\n`env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` in `ADV`, run three times, each time:\n\n```\nFAIL  tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts > command routing slice\nError: @spec-kit/system-skill-advisor dist is stale (source content differs from the attested build). Rebuild with: cd .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime && npm run build\n ❯ scoreCommandCorpus scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:443:13\n ❯ tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:112:12\n Test Files  1 failed (1)\n      Tests  6 skipped (6)\n```\n\n`env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD node .../scratch/planning/probe-capture-env.mjs` from the root fails on the same stale-dist error at `scoreCommandCorpus` line 443.\n\n**What I could not do**\n\n- The test-first failure on `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR` was never observable. The capture throws on the freshness gate before the new case runs. The suite did parse the edited test file and reached `beforeAll`, so the TypeScript is valid. `node --check` on the capture script exits 0.\n- The stale dist is caused by other lanes' uncommitted edits to `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` and `runtime/lib/subprocess.ts`. `before.txt` records the setup build as `exit=0`, so the dist was fresh when T001 ran. Workers may not run a build, so I did not rebuild.\n- As a diagnostic only, I ran the capture in a throwaway process with `checkPackageFreshness` stubbed in memory. It printed `variables left changed: []`, and its four floor lines matched `before.txt` exactly (`24/44`, `0/35`, `44/44`, `28/45`). This is not the task verify and does not replace it.\n\nThe coordinator needs to rebuild `@spec-kit/system-skill-advisor` (`npm run build` in `ADV`) and rerun T014's `VX` and probe once the other `lib/` lanes have stopped editing. I did not tick the checkbox and touched no other file.","time":{"start":1794589779156,"end":1794589787269}}}
